<Base title="About" description="Rio Gonzales started in computer engineering, built a career in HR and analytics, and is returning to engineering.">
  <section class="page-head wrap">
    <p class="label accent">About</p>
    <h1>I’ve always been wired to be technical</h1>
  </section>

  <div class="prose wrap">
    <p>
      I’m Rio Gonzales. I started college studying computer engineering, with the goal of becoming a hardware engineer.
      Life had other plans. I switched to Business Administration, and an internship led me into human resources.
    </p>
    <p>
      I built a career there. Today I’m an HR Director and a SHRM Senior Certified Professional, with a master’s degree
      in Business Analytics. The part of that work I’ve enjoyed most is using data to make better decisions about people.
    </p>

    <h2>The thread that never broke</h2>
    <p>
      The interest in technology and complex systems was there long before the career. As a child I read books about
      military vehicles and aircraft. As a teenager I built desktop computers. In college I built cryptocurrency mining
      rigs. These days I work on computers, cars and software projects.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’ve come to accept that this is how I’m wired, and that I need to follow it. Technical work feeds my soul.
    </p>

    <h2>Where I’m headed</h2>
    <p>
      My focus now is AI and machine learning, computing, and hardware. In January 2027 I begin a bachelor’s degree in
      Electrical Engineering at Arizona State University, while continuing to work full-time.
      The <a href="/journey/">Journey</a> page tracks what I’m doing now and what’s next,
      and <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> shows what I’m building.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
